<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2841" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄκαινα</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ης</span>, ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκή</span> A,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκίς</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>spike, prick, goad</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				3.1323
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				6.41
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Agath.
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>ten-foot rod</i> used as a measure, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄκαιναν ἀμφότερον κέντρον τε βοῶν καὶ
					μέτρον ἀρούρης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Call.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					214
				</span></i>
			, cf. Sch.<i><span class="en">
				A.R.
			</span></i> l.c. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>square measure of 100 ft.</i>, in Egypt, <i><span class="en">
				Hero
			</span></i>
			<i>*Deff.</i><i><span class="en">
				130
			</span></i>, cf. Sch. A.R.l.c., <i><span class="en">
				<u>POxy.</u>
				669.41
			</span></i> (? <span class="entity">iii A. D.</span>); in Bithynia, <i><span class="en">
				<u>BCH</u>
				27.318
			</span></i>:— also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄκαινον</span></b> , τό, <i><span class="en">
				Olymp.
				<u>in Mete</u>
				43.1
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
